{"id":"QB-261113-CZVP","title":"Hoang Pham · 13/11 · Composite, implicit & inverse, Limits & continuity","student":"Hoang Pham","questions":[{"id":"APCALCBC-STPAULHANOI-U2U3-TEST-V1-Q09","ref":"APCALCBC-STPAULHANOI-U2U3-TEST-V1-Q09","label":"1","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"Find $f''(x)$ if $f(x)=3x^5-6x^2$.","options":{"A":"$f''(x)=180x^2$","B":"$f''(x)=3x^5-12x^2$","C":"$f''(x)=60x^3-12$","D":"$f''(x)=15x^4-12x$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-BC-1-MCQ-Q26","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-BC-1-MCQ-Q26","label":"2","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"If $f^{\\prime}(x)=h(x)$ and $g(x)=x^3$, then $\\dfrac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=$","options":{"A":"$h(x^3)$","B":"$3x^2h(x)$","C":"$3x^2h(x^3)$","D":"$h(3x^2)$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q22","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q22","label":"3","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"Assume $y$ is a differentiable function of $x$. For $x+\\cos(x+y)=0$, choose $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$.","options":{"A":"$\\csc(x+y)-1$","B":"$\\csc(x+y)$","C":"$\\dfrac{x}{\\sin(x+y)}$","D":"$\\dfrac{1-\\sin x}{\\sin y}$"}},{"id":"APCALCAB-2024INT-MCQ-Q01","ref":"APCALCAB-2024INT-MCQ-Q01","label":"4","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\left(x^2-11x+24\\right)^7\\right)=$","options":{"A":"$7(2x-11)^6$","B":"$7(2x-11)^6\\left(x^2-11x+24\\right)$","C":"$7\\left(x^2-11x+24\\right)^6$","D":"$7\\left(x^2-11x+24\\right)^6(2x-11)$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-BC-1-MCQ-Q05","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-PRACTICETEST-BC-1-MCQ-Q05","label":"5","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"$$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x&f(x)&f^{\\prime}(x)&g(x)&g^{\\prime}(x)\\\\\\hline 1&2&1/2&-3&5\\\\2&3&1&0&4\\\\3&4&2&2&3\\\\4&6&4&3&1/2\\\\\\hline\\end{array}$$\n\nThe table shows values of differentiable functions $f$ and $g$. If $h(x)=g(f(x))$, then $h^{\\prime}(3)=$","options":{"A":"$\\frac12$","B":"$1$","C":"$4$","D":"$6$"}},{"id":"AI-0499a","ref":"AI-0499a","label":"6","marks":3,"calculator":false,"stem":"The functions $f$ and $g$ are defined by $f(x)=\\begin{cases}2x-1 & x<3\\\\ 4 & x=3\\\\ x+2 & x>3\\end{cases}$ and $g(x)=\\begin{cases}x-1 & x<3\\\\ 2 & x=3\\\\ 5-x & x>3\\end{cases}$. Let $h(x)=(6-f(x))\\,g(x)$.\n\nFind $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to3}h(x)$, showing the one-sided limits."},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q60","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q60","label":"7","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"If $f(x)=\\dfrac1{x^2+1}$ and $g(x)=\\sqrt x$, the derivative of $f(g(x))$ is","options":{"A":"$-(x+1)^{-2}$","B":"$\\dfrac{-2x}{(x^2+1)^2}$","C":"$\\dfrac1{(x+1)^2}$","D":"$\\dfrac1{2\\sqrt x(x+1)}$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3B-Q23","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3B-Q23","label":"8","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Suppose $f(1)=2$, $f^{\\prime}(1)=3$, and $f^{\\prime}(2)=4$. Then $(f^{-1})^{\\prime}(2)$","options":{"A":"equals $-\\frac13$","B":"equals $-\\frac14$","C":"equals $\\frac14$","D":"equals $\\frac13$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q28","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q28","label":"9","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"Which of the following functions does not have an inverse function?","options":{"A":"$y=\\sin x\\ \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le x\\le\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$","B":"$y=x^3+2$","C":"$y=\\frac{x}{x^2+1}$","D":"$y=\\ln(x-2)$ (where $x>2$)"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q45","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q45","label":"10","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"If $\\sin(xy)=x$, then $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=$","options":{"A":"$\\dfrac{\\sec(xy)}x$","B":"$\\dfrac{\\sec(xy)-y}x$","C":"$\\dfrac{1+\\sec(xy)}x$","D":"$\\sec(xy)-1$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q26","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q26","label":"11","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"$\\tan\\left(\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\right)=$","options":{"A":"$-1$","B":"$-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","C":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$","D":"$1$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH2B-Q04","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH2B-Q04","label":"12","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"The function $f(x)=\\begin{cases}\\dfrac{x^2}{x} & (x\\neq 0)\\\\[2mm] 0 & (x=0)\\end{cases}$","options":{"A":"is continuous everywhere","B":"is continuous except at $x=0$","C":"has a removable discontinuity at $x=0$","D":"has an infinite discontinuity at $x=0$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q14","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q14","label":"13","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"For $y=\\sin\\dfrac1x$, choose the derivative $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$.","options":{"A":"$\\cos\\dfrac1x$","B":"$\\cos\\left(-\\dfrac1{x^2}\\right)$","C":"$-\\dfrac1{x^2}\\cos\\dfrac1x$","D":"$-\\dfrac1{x^2}\\sin\\dfrac1x+\\dfrac1x\\cos\\dfrac1x$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q29","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q29","label":"14","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"Suppose that $f(x)=\\ln x$ for all positive $x$ and $g(x)=9-x^2$ for all real $x$.\n\nThe domain of $f(g(x))$ is","options":{"A":"$\\{x\\mid x\\le 3\\}$","B":"$\\{x\\mid |x|>3\\}$","C":"$\\{x\\mid |x|<3\\}$","D":"$\\{x\\mid 0<x<3\\}$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3B-Q04","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3B-Q04","label":"15","marks":1,"calculator":true,"stem":"Differentiable functions $f$ and $g$ have the following values, paired in order: $$\\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|c|} \\hline x & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ \\hline f(x) & 2 & 3 & 5 & 10 \\\\ \\hline f'(x) & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline g(x) & 5 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\hline g'(x) & -4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}$$\n\nIf $H(x)=\\sqrt{f(x)}$, then $H^{\\prime}(3)=$","options":{"A":"$\\dfrac14$","B":"$\\dfrac1{2\\sqrt{10}}$","C":"$\\dfrac2{\\sqrt{10}}$","D":"$4\\sqrt{10}$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q43","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH3A-Q43","label":"16","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"If $h$ is the inverse of $f$ and $f(x)=1/x$, then $h^{\\prime}(3)=$","options":{"A":"$-9$","B":"$-\\dfrac19$","C":"$\\dfrac19$","D":"$9$"}},{"id":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q08","ref":"APCALC-BARRONS27-CH1A-Q08","label":"17","marks":1,"calculator":false,"stem":"Let $g$ be a function defined for all reals. Which of the following conditions is not sufficient to guarantee that $g$ has an inverse function?","options":{"A":"$g(x) = ax + b$, $a \\neq 0$","B":"$g$ is strictly decreasing","C":"$g$ is symmetric to the origin","D":"$g$ is one-to-one"}}]}